Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant table & columns for the task  
(bigquery‑public‑data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_representation)

• `workforce` : filter to overall workforce (`workforce = 'overall'`).  
• `report_year` : pick the two end‑points 2014 and 2024.  
• `race_asian` : percent Asians – to compute growth.  
• `race_black` : percent Black – to compute growth.  
• `race_hispanic_latinx` : percent Latinx – to compute growth.  
• `race_native_american` : percent Native American – to compute growth.  
• `race_white` : percent White – to compute growth.  
• `gender_us_women` : percent U.S. women – to compute growth.  
• `gender_us_men` : percent U.S. men – to compute growth.  
• `gender_global_women` : percent global women – to compute growth.  
• `gender_global_men` : percent global men – to compute growth.  

Typical WHERE conditions that will be useful  
```sql
WHERE workforce = 'overall'
  AND report_year BETWEEN 2014 AND 2024          -- or = 2014 / 2024
```

Below are ten exploratory‑to‑final SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that one could run in BigQuery to inspect the data step‑by‑step and then obtain the requested growth‑rates.

```sql
-- Description: 1) Peek at all available workforce groups in the table
SELECT DISTINCT `workforce`
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_representation`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 2) Look at the 2014 overall‑workforce representation record
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_representation`
WHERE workforce = 'overall'
  AND report_year = 2014
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 3) Look at the 2024 overall‑workforce representation record
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_representation`
WHERE workforce = 'overall'
  AND report_year = 2024
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 4) Retrieve all yearly values (2014‑2024) for Asians in the overall workforce
SELECT report_year,
       race_asian
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_representation`
WHERE workforce = 'overall'
  AND report_year BETWEEN 2014 AND 2024
ORDER BY report_year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 5) Same as #4 but for U.S. women
SELECT report_year,
       gender_us_women
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_representation`
WHERE workforce = 'overall'
  AND report_year BETWEEN 2014 AND 2024
ORDER BY report_year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 6) Put the two end‑points side‑by‑side (2014 vs 2024) for race columns
SELECT 
  a.report_year  AS year_2014,
  b.report_year  AS year_2024,
  a.race_asian        AS asian_2014,
  b.race_asian        AS asian_2024,
  a.race_black        AS black_2014,
  b.race_black        AS black_2024,
  a.race_hispanic_latinx AS latinx_2014,
  b.race_hispanic_latinx AS latinx_2024,
  a.race_native_american AS native_2014,
  b.race_native_american AS native_2024,
  a.race_white        AS white_2014,
  b.race_white        AS white_2024
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_representation` AS a
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_representation` AS b
  USING (workforce)
WHERE a.workforce = 'overall'
  AND a.report_year = 2014
  AND b.report_year = 2024
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 7) Compute growth‑rates for the race columns
SELECT
  (b.race_asian - a.race_asian) / a.race_asian        AS asian_growth_rate,
  (b.race_black - a.race_black) / a.race_black        AS black_growth_rate,
  (b.race_hispanic_latinx - a.race_hispanic_latinx) / a.race_hispanic_latinx  AS latinx_growth_rate,
  (b.race_native_american - a.race_native_american) / a.race_native_american  AS native_growth_rate,
  (b.race_white - a.race_white) / a.race_white        AS white_growth_rate
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_representation` AS a
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_representation` AS b
  USING (workforce)
WHERE a.workforce = 'overall'
  AND a.report_year = 2014
  AND b.report_year = 2024
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 8) Compute growth‑rates for U.S. and global gender columns
SELECT
  (b.gender_us_women - a.gender_us_women) / a.gender_us_women       AS us_women_growth_rate,
  (b.gender_us_men   - a.gender_us_men)   / a.gender_us_men         AS us_men_growth_rate,
  (b.gender_global_women - a.gender_global_women) / a.gender_global_women AS global_women_growth_rate,
  (b.gender_global_men   - a.gender_global_men)   / a.gender_global_men   AS global_men_growth_rate
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_representation` AS a
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_representation` AS b
  USING (workforce)
WHERE a.workforce = 'overall'
  AND a.report_year = 2014
  AND b.report_year = 2024
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- Description: 9) One‑row summary: race + gender growth‑rates together
SELECT
  (b.race_asian - a.race_asian) / a.race_asian                         AS asian_growth_rate,
  (b.race_black - a.race_black) / a.race_black                         AS black_growth_rate,
  (b.race_hispanic_latinx - a.race_hispanic_latinx) / a.race_hispanic_latinx AS latinx_growth_rate,
  (b.race_native_american - a.race_native_american) / a.race_native_american AS native_growth_rate,
  (b.race_white - a.race_white) / a.race_white                         AS white_growth_rate,
  (b.gender_us_women - a.gender_us_women) / a.gender_us_women          AS us_women_growth_rate,
  (b.gender_us_men   - a.gender_us_men)   / a.gender_us_men            AS us_men_growth_rate,
  (b.gender_global_women - a.gender_global_women) / a.gender_global_women AS global_women_growth_rate,
  (b.gender_global_men   - a.gender_global_men)   / a.gender_global_men   AS global_men_growth_rate
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_representation` AS a
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.google_dei.dar_non_intersectional_representation` AS b
  USING (workforce)
WHERE a.workforce = 'overall'
  AND a.report_year = 2014
  AND b.report_year = 2024
LIMIT 20;
```

